5. Which reflections preserve Z?  iota_s(x) = (s-4)/(s-2) - x maps Z to Z iff (s-2) | 2
====================================================================================================
  s= 3  iota(x) = -1 - x   centre -1/2   integral: True   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s= 4  iota(x) = 0 - x   centre 0   integral: True   centre in Z_2: True   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s= 5  iota(x) = 1/3 - x   centre 1/6   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s= 6  iota(x) = 1/2 - x   centre 1/4   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: False
  s= 7  iota(x) = 3/5 - x   centre 3/10   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s= 8  iota(x) = 2/3 - x   centre 1/3   integral: False   centre in Z_2: True   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s= 9  iota(x) = 5/7 - x   centre 5/14   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s=10  iota(x) = 3/4 - x   centre 3/8   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: False
  s=11  iota(x) = 7/9 - x   centre 7/18   integral: False   centre in Z_2: False   iota preserves Z_2: True
  s=12  iota(x) = 4/5 - x   centre 2/5   integral: False   centre in Z_2: True   iota preserves Z_2: True
  centres: s=3 -> -1/2 = fixed point of x -> 3x+1 ;  s=4 -> 0 = fixed point of x -> 3x
  rule q x + d has centre -d/(q-1); its reflection x -> -2d/(q-1) - x preserves Z iff (q-1) | 2d:
     3x+1: reflection x -> -1 - x   integral: True
     3x-1: reflection x -> 1 - x   integral: True
     5x+1: reflection x -> -1/2 - x   integral: False
     5x-1: reflection x -> 1/2 - x   integral: False
     7x+1: reflection x -> -1/3 - x   integral: False
     5x+3: reflection x -> -3/2 - x   integral: False
     9x+1: reflection x -> -1/4 - x   integral: False

